Q: Hide right Sidebar of JIRA A: <p>In Edge you can add Bookmarks which can use javascript code that acts on the site you are on.</p>
<ol>
<li><p>Add a new Bookmark</p>
</li>
<li><p>Give it a name (i named mine &quot;&lt;&gt;&quot;)</p>
</li>
<li><p>add the code to URL:</p>
</li>
</ol>
<pre><code>javascript:(
    function(){
        var issue_sidebar = document.getElementById(&quot;viewissuesidebar&quot;);
        if (issue_sidebar.style.display != &quot;none&quot;) {
            issue_sidebar.style.display = &quot;none&quot;;
        } else {
            var issue_sidebar = document.getElementById(&quot;viewissuesidebar&quot;);
            issue_sidebar.style.display = &quot;&quot;;
        }
    }
)();
</code></pre>
<p>this assumes the sidebar on the right has ID &quot;viewissuesidebar&quot;</p>
<p>When you have a JIRA Ticket opened and click on the Bookmark, it will toggle the Sidebar ON/OFF and hence make the Content Fields width maximum</p>

Q: XSLT unparsed-text() URL resolution issued A: <p>I have cross-compiled the current version of Saxon HE, Saxon HE 12, to .NET with a modern version of IKVM that might not have such problems as it uses a more up to date OpenJDK, NuGet package is <a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/SaxonHE12s9apiExtensions" rel="nofollow noreferrer">SaxonHE12s9apiExtensions</a>, here is some sample code</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>using System;
using System.IO;

using net.liberty_development.SaxonHE12s9apiExtensions;
using net.sf.saxon.s9api;


namespace SaxonHE12TestUnparsedTextHTTPAccess2
{
    internal class Program
    {
        static void Main(string[] args)
        {
            var processor = new Processor();

            var xsltCompiler = processor.newXsltCompiler();

            var xsltExecutable = xsltCompiler.Compile(new FileInfo(&quot;sheet1.xsl&quot;));

            var xslt30Transformer = xsltExecutable.load30();

            xslt30Transformer.callTemplate(null, processor.NewSerializer(Console.Out));

        }
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>Project file for .NET/VS needs to modern project style as the modern IKVM only works with that project style:</p>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;Project Sdk=&quot;Microsoft.NET.Sdk&quot;&gt;

  &lt;PropertyGroup&gt;
    &lt;OutputType&gt;Exe&lt;/OutputType&gt;
    &lt;TargetFramework&gt;net481&lt;/TargetFramework&gt;
  &lt;/PropertyGroup&gt;

  &lt;ItemGroup&gt;
    &lt;PackageReference Include=&quot;SaxonHE12s9apiExtensions&quot; Version=&quot;12.9.10&quot; /&gt;
  &lt;/ItemGroup&gt;

  &lt;ItemGroup&gt;
    &lt;None Update=&quot;sheet1.xsl&quot;&gt;
      &lt;CopyToOutputDirectory&gt;PreserveNewest&lt;/CopyToOutputDirectory&gt;
    &lt;/None&gt;
  &lt;/ItemGroup&gt;

&lt;/Project&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Sample sheet1.xsl can access your HTTPS URL without problems does e.g.</p>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;xsl:stylesheet xmlns:xsl=&quot;http://www.w3.org/1999/XSL/Transform&quot; version=&quot;3.0&quot;&gt;
    &lt;xsl:template name=&quot;xsl:initial-template&quot;&gt;
        &lt;xsl:value-of select=&quot;unparsed-text('https://code.jquery.com/jquery-3.5.1.min.js')&quot;/&gt;
    &lt;/xsl:template&gt;
&lt;/xsl:stylesheet&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>I realize that is not a direct answer to your problem with the old Saxon HE 10 .NET library but I think the problem is caused by its use of an old/outdated IKVM using an old/outdated JDK, so updating to a more modern stack of Saxon/IKVM/the underlying JDK can avoid the problem.</p>
